  "prompt": "[system]\n\n    You generate compact, robust Python TSP metaheuristics.\n    You must follow the requested interface exactly, always preserve tour validity.\n    \n\n[user]\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000019: farthest_first_improve_2opt\n\nStatus: valid; distance: 8.28027\n\nThought: Farthest-insertion construction then first-improving 2-opt local search.\n\nCode:\n\n```python\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = len(distance_matrix)\n    if n <= 2:\n        tour = np.arange(n)\n        report_best_tour(tour)\n        return tour\n\n    def total_distance(tour):\n        return distance_matrix[tour, np.roll(tour, -1)].sum()\n\n    # Farthest insertion construction\n    start = 0\n    end = np.argmax(distance_matrix[start])\n    tour = [start, end]\n    in_tour = {start, end}\n    while len(tour) < n:\n        best_node = -1\n        best_dist = -1.0\n        for node in range(n):\n            if node in in_tour:\n                continue\n            min_dist = min(distance_matrix[node, t] for t in tour)\n            if min_dist > best_dist:\n                best_dist = min_dist\n                best_node = node\n        best_pos = -1\n        best_increase = float('inf')\n        for i in range(len(tour)):\n            a = tour[i]\n            b = tour[(i+1)%len(tour)]\n            increase = distance_matrix[a, best_node] + distance_matrix[best_node, b] - distance_matrix[a, b]\n            if increase < best_increase:\n                best_increase = increase\n                best_pos = i+1\n        tour.insert(best_pos, best_node)\n        in_tour.add(best_node)\n    best_tour = tour[:]\n    best_cost = total_distance(best_tour)\n    report_best_tour(np.array(best_tour))\n\n    # First-improving 2-opt local search\n    improved = True\n    while improved:\n        improved = False\n        for i in range(n-2):\n            for j in range(i+2, n):\n                if i == 0 and j == n-1:\n                    continue\n                a, b = tour[i], tour[(i+1)%n]\n                c, d = tour[j], tour[(j+1)%n]\n                delta = distance_matrix[a, c] + distance_matrix[b, d] - distance_matrix[a, b] - distance_matrix[c, d]\n                if delta < -1e-12:\n                    tour = tour[:i+1] + tour[i+1:j+1][::-1] + tour[j+1:]\n                    new_cost = best_cost + delta\n                    if new_cost < best_cost - 1e-12:\n                        best_cost = new_cost\n                        best_tour = tour[:]\n                        report_best_tour(np.array(best_tour))\n                    improved = True\n                    break\n            if improved:\n                break\n    return np.array(best_tour)\n\n```\n\nVERBAL GRADIENT: follow the reflection below as the primary source of change.\n\nUse the supplied parents as supporting evidence only.\n\nPARENT-SPECIFIC LLM REFLECTIONS:\n\nParent cand_000019 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Candidate uses farthest insertion plus first-improving 2-opt; it runs faster but yields slightly longer tours than the parent with steepest 2-opt and ILS.\n- Aim: Reduce tour length to match or surpass the parent while keeping runtime moderate and retaining 100% validity.\n- Preserve: fast first-improving 2-opt; farthest insertion construction; report_best_tour usage\n- Change: Add a limited iterated local search (e.g., a few random 2-opt perturbations followed by first-improving 2-opt) to escape local optima\n- Avoid: Switching to steepest 2-opt (risk of timeout); removing construction heuristic; adding complex neighborhoods that may break validity\n\nDistance is the search objective for TSP; lower distance is better.\n\nImplement a complete TSP metaheuristic inside this required entrypoint:\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n\nRequirements:\n- Minimize total TSP tour distance.\n- Return a 1D np.ndarray containing each node exactly once.\n- Do not repeat the start node at the end.\n